%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: bcb78f8a433e42cb8b63774b6a2ddb9c, type: 3}
  m_Name: DivineAudienceScript
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DivineAudienceScript
  deities:
  - type: 1
    deityName: Kethra
    epithet: the Undying Coal
    presence: The dark takes fire. A storm of it, turning where no wind could reach,
      and the stone does not burn.
    backdrop: {fileID: 0}
    overrideTint: 0
    tint: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
    inserts:
    - tier: 1
      line: Fire does not ask what it is given. It takes the room. Take the room.
    - tier: 2
      line: Every coal I have ever been was somebody's hearth first. Warmth and ruin
        are one act at different speeds.
    - tier: 3
      line: You have burned steadily. I have watched better fires go out from being
        careful.
    - tier: 4
      line: There is no last coal. There is only the next thing dry enough.
  - type: 2
    deityName: Ollu
    epithet: the Drowned Mouth
    presence: Water where there was air. It turns slowly, all the way down, and something
      is looking up through it.
    backdrop: {fileID: 0}
    overrideTint: 0
    tint: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
    inserts:
    - tier: 1
      line: Water is patient because water always wins. Learn the first half; the
        second is arithmetic.
    - tier: 2
      line: I have taken more of them than fire ever did. Quietly. Not one saw the
        moment it became too late.
    - tier: 3
      line: Everything that drowns keeps its shape a while. So do you.
    - tier: 4
      line: The deep has no floor. It has a place where you stop being able to tell.
  - type: 3
    deityName: Vaun
    epithet: the Long Breath
    presence: The rock opens on a sky. Cloud, lit from behind, moving far too fast
      to be weather.
    backdrop: {fileID: 0}
    overrideTint: 0
    tint: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
    inserts:
    - tier: 1
      line: They think of me as the open sky. I am also the air in a sealed room,
        going bad.
    - tier: 2
      line: Nothing I do leaves a mark. Ask them how well that has protected them.
    - tier: 3
      line: You are the only one of mine that has been underground this long and
        still moved.
    - tier: 4
      line: Breathe out. Everything above you is downwind now.
  - type: 4
    deityName: Morrun
    epithet: the Weight Below
    presence: The walls do not move, and still they lean. The whole weight of the
      world is paying attention.
    backdrop: {fileID: 0}
    overrideTint: 0
    tint: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
    inserts:
    - tier: 1
      line: Stone does not hurry and stone is never late. You have been hurrying.
        Stop.
    - tier: 2
      line: I am what lies under their fields, their roads and their graves. They
        stand on me and call it their country.
    - tier: 3
      line: Three floors of mine you have opened. I felt each one the way a man feels
        a splinter go in.
    - tier: 4
      line: You were always going to be mine. Everything is, eventually. You are
        simply early.
  - type: 5
    deityName: Ussar
    epithet: the Unlit
    presence: The dark deepens until it has an edge. The edge turns.
    backdrop: {fileID: 0}
    overrideTint: 0
    tint: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
    inserts:
    - tier: 1
      line: There was dark before there was anything for it to be dark against. Mine
        is the older claim.
    - tier: 2
      line: They bring lights down here. That is the whole of their courage. A lamp,
        and each other.
    - tier: 3
      line: You have made a place where their light does not help them. That is my
        work, done with your hands.
    - tier: 4
      line: Put out the last of it. I do not need to be seen to be attended.
  - type: 6
    deityName: Ienna
    epithet: the Buried Sun
    presence: Light climbs out of the floor. It is under the stone. It always was.
    backdrop: {fileID: 0}
    overrideTint: 0
    tint: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
    inserts:
    - tier: 1
      line: Their light falls on things. Mine comes up through them. Do not confuse
        us.
    - tier: 2
      line: The Church took my name and hung it in the sky where nobody could reach
        it. Down here it still answers.
    - tier: 3
      line: What is buried is not extinguished. You are the standing proof, and they
        have begun to notice.
    - tier: 4
      line: Rise, then. Not into their sky. Through it.
  tiers:
  - tier: 1
    opening:
    - I am {god}. They called me {epithet}, when they still called me anything.
    - You are noticed. That is not a kindness. It is a fact, and you will live inside
      it now.
    - What you have been pulling up out of the dark has a source. It is me. Every
      claimed stone, every death you kept -- mine, and I let you take it.
    closing:
    - Take more, then. Not the power. Power is easy, and it makes fools of easy things.
      Take the knowing that comes attached to it. That is the part they could not
      seal.
    - A stair is yours to cut. Go down. What answers you at that depth did not answer
      you here.
    - Descend. I am under you the whole way.
  - tier: 2
    opening:
    - Again. Sooner than the last, with more of them in the ground behind you.
    - You siphon well now. I feel it the way a man feels a cut he did not notice
      taking. Steadily, and from somewhere he cannot see.
    closing:
    - Understand what you take, servant. Not my strength. My memory. Everything of
      mine ever put down in the dark left its shape in me, and you are drawing those
      shapes up through your own floor.
    - Cut your stair. What waits below has been waiting since the sealing.
    - Go. Take what is mine and make a wall of it.
  - tier: 3
    opening:
    - Three times. There were centuries when none of mine came this far.
    - The Church calls this theft. They called it theft when it was done to them,
      then they did it to us, then they wrote the word down and left it pointing
      at you.
    closing:
    - You are close enough now to be told plainly. Nothing above ground made you.
      You were dead, the deep kept you, and what you draw out of me is the substance
      you are made of. This is not theft. You are eating at home.
    - One more floor will answer you. And then something comes that was assembled
      out of everything you have angered. I do not intervene. You will meet it as
      I met mine.
    - Survive it. Then we speak as we have never spoken.
  - tier: 4
    opening:
    - You survived it. Stand. There is no kneeling left in this.
    - You have taken so much of me that I can no longer say where the siphon ends.
      That is not a complaint. It is what the faith was for, and what the sealing
      was meant to prevent.
    closing:
    - 'So: the last of the knowing. There is no rank above this one. What comes now
      is not measured and not earned. It is yours, the way the dark is mine.'
    - The deep is open to its floor, and nothing above is coming for you any more.
      They spent what they had. They know it.
    - Take it, and be what I am. I am under you the whole way.
